1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:04,190
Did you manage to tell your 
grandma the truth about us?

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,400
I couldn't.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,320
I tried to, but she said 
she was fine either way.

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:14,120
When she said that, I just couldn't 
bring myself to tell her.

5
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:16,620
I don't regret it, though.

6
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:18,290
I mean it.

7
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:22,040
That dilemma helped me consider 
what I was doing for her,

8
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:24,050
and what was for myself,

9
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,450
right until the very end.

10
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:29,200
And I'm thankful that 
you presented it to me.

11
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:34,920
But also, it's made it harder 
to come clean...

12
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:39,700
If we tell Granny Nagomi the truth now,

13
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:45,370
she'll despise us for lying to my 
grandma until her last breath.

14
00:00:46,570 --> 00:00:49,220
I won't let that happen.

15
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:53,950
I swear I'll protect you from the blame!

16
00:00:58,420 --> 00:00:59,760
How, exactly?

17
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,330
I thought I was good at going it alone

18
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,330
Would you prefer to go together?

19
00:02:07,150 --> 00:02:07,860
Place
your finger here

20
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,000
Rent-a-Girlfriend

21
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:34,510
"Climax and Girlfriend"

22
00:02:34,770 --> 00:02:38,260
Sayuri-san believed in youâ€”

23
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:43,440
that her dear granddaughter introduced 
a boyfriend to her for the first time.

24
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:47,760
And I'm sure she believed 
it to her dying breath.

25
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:52,070
If what Mami-dono says is true,

26
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:56,200
then I can overlook anything but the 
fact that you lied to my late friend.

27
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,080
I would like to believe 
that this is all a mistake.

28
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,950
Is there anything you can 
say in your defense?

29
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:16,280
<i>There's nothing we can say! 
Because we did lie!</i>

30
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:21,470
<i>No! Mizuhara was torn up over it!</i>

31
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:24,850
<i>She just barely missed her 
chance to tell the truth, is all!</i>

32
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:30,740
<i>But whatever we say now, 
after lying for a year and a half,</i>

33
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,130
<i>it'll only sound like an excuse.</i>

34
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:35,180
<i>It's not fair!</i>

35
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:40,030
<i>I mean, Sayuri-san isn't here 
to stand up for her.</i>

36
00:03:40,830 --> 00:03:43,920
<i>There's nothing we can do anymore.</i>

37
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:10,940
I see.

38
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,680
Never mind.

39
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:16,350
We're done.

40
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:22,210
I'm tired now.

41
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,420
No...

42
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:37,570
No...

43
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,920
You've got it all wrong, guys.

44
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:51,510
<i>If you had to pick the worst declaration 
of love in human history,</i>

45
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:53,230
<i>it'd have to be this moment here.</i>

46
00:04:54,470 --> 00:05:00,280
<i>Before I knew it, that outpouring 
of emotion had escaped my lips.</i>

47
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:06,800
<i>It was like charging into a gunfight 
with nothing but a matchstick.</i>

48
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:10,800
Mizuhara's not that kind of person.

49
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:14,930
I'm telling you, 
you've got it all wrong...

50
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:18,500
Gran... everyone...

51
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:24,050
<i>It was a last-ditch effort that 
was desperately uncool.</i>

52
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:28,080
<i>This pathetic white knight's 
final lie began to unfold.</i>

53
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:32,520
I mean... we really are together.

54
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,980
Mami-chan doesn't know,

55
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:39,690
but a week or so before 
Granny Sayuri passed away,

56
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:41,960
we started dating for real.

57
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:47,020
So it was more like Chizuru 
had no reason to tell her.

58
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,910
I mean, it would've been weird to tell her

59
00:05:49,910 --> 00:05:52,840
that we lied, but only 
until a week before.

60
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:58,300
So yeah, ultimately, 
Chizuru didn't lie to Sayuri-san.

61
00:05:58,660 --> 00:05:59,520
Okay?

62
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,980
Have you thought this through?

63
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:16,010
I hope you realize 
what you're trying to do.

64
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,170
Lie here, and you're done for.

65
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:22,880
It's curtains!

66
00:06:24,730 --> 00:06:27,660
<i>Sorry... I'm sorry, Kibe!</i>

67
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,620
<i>I get it.</i>

68
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:33,120
<i>I've seen how much you care about me!</i>

69
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:35,320
<i>You've made it clear as day!</i>

70
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:41,550
I told you, Mizuhara's 
not that kind of person.

71
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:44,950
<i>But I can't! I just can't!</i>

72
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:45,180
She deceived you all?

73
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:47,430
You've gotta be kidding me.

74
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:53,230
<i>You know there's nothing else I could do!</i>

75
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:52,620
She's a lovely girl through and through.

76
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:58,070
She's always sincere and lives life 
with her head held high.

77
00:06:58,070 --> 00:07:00,360
<i>I don't care if I look pathetic,</i>

78
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:03,070
<i>or if you all end up thinking 
I'm a total piece of trash.</i>

79
00:07:01,030 --> 00:07:05,250
And she loved Sayuri-san 
from the bottom of her heart.

80
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:10,820
<i>I just can't handle anyone 
thinking badly of her!</i>

81
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:10,480
I was obviously at fault for everything.

82
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:12,490
<i>That's the one thing I can't deal with!</i>

83
00:07:15,890 --> 00:07:17,920
She's a gentle soul.

84
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:22,120
She kept this all a secret for my sake.

85
00:07:23,030 --> 00:07:25,950
<i>I can just say we broke up 
once we get back to Tokyo!</i>

86
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:28,780
<i>If anyone has to lie, let it be me!</i>

87
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:33,600
<i>Even as all this is happening, I feel 
so bad for putting her in this position.</i>

88
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:35,790
She'll despise us...

89
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:38,200
<i>After all, I swore to 
protect her from the blame!</i>

90
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:41,000
<i>And I'm gonna see it through!</i>

91
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:44,540
She's always pretty,

92
00:07:45,430 --> 00:07:48,600
kind, and the coolest person alive.

93
00:07:50,430 --> 00:07:55,530
That's the Mizuhara Chizuru 
I've come to love!

94
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:13,850
Kiss, then.

95
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,980
Prove it by kissing.

96
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:25,960
Huh?

97
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,950
Rent-a-Girlfriend

98
00:08:28,950 --> 00:08:31,570
Cursed Mansion

99
00:08:30,170 --> 00:08:31,570
Hey, Ruka.

100
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:38,750
You were out already, huh? 
Wasn't that thrilling?

101
00:08:40,650 --> 00:08:44,210
Yep, my heart was racing! It was so good!

102
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:47,670
Right? Yumi even froze up 
in the middle there.

103
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:51,450
Can you blame me? I was so startled.

104
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:54,510
<i>To say it was 24/7/365 
would be a bit overboard,</i>

105
00:08:51,450 --> 00:08:53,410
That was too scary.

106
00:08:55,140 --> 00:09:00,480
<i>but I'd say I spent 
24/7/364 searching for it.</i>

107
00:09:02,150 --> 00:09:05,980
<i>No matter when or where, 
it always occupied a corner of my mind.</i>

108
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:11,800
<i>Because I felt like the universe 
was telling me I was defective.</i>

109
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:16,620
May my illness be cured soon
- Sarashina Ruka, Class 2-3

110
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:16,620
<i>I only ever made one wish on Tanabata...</i>

111
00:09:17,110 --> 00:09:24,140
<i>So when I found you, you really felt
like a knight in shining armor.</i>

112
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:24,710
She may be a rental, but Mizuhara is...

113
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,210
the best girlfriend anyone could ask for!

114
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:38,900
<i>I truly thought you'd be the prince
to bring color into my life.</i>

115
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:47,770
<i>But you were in love with someone.</i>

116
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:51,400
<i>Someone very beautiful,</i>

117
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:53,060
<i>and very mature.</i>

118
00:09:54,050 --> 00:09:57,500
<i>There was never a moment when 
I thought I had the upper hand.</i>

119
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:01,160
<i>That's why I'd get so anxious 
every now and then.</i>

120
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:05,710
Congrats on our eight-month, 
ten-day anniversary!

121
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,750
Shouldn't we be more selective?

122
00:10:07,750 --> 00:10:10,280
Hey, it's also our 250th day as a couple!

123
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:11,210
Even that doesn't feel
too significant

124
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:16,430
Maritozzi taste so good 
when you're with your beloved!

125
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:18,110
Yo, check her out.

126
00:10:18,110 --> 00:10:19,080
She's so cute!

127
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,850
She's so slender and fair!

128
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:22,740
We're just getting started.

129
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:24,840
Today, we're hitting the cinema, 
the Ferris wheel,

130
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:28,020
and so many other things 
I've been looking forward to!

131
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:32,140
But seriously, 
what are you planning to do?

132
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:32,860
Huh?

133
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:39,160
You can't tell your family a rental 
girlfriend is your partner forever.

134
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:43,330
I mean, your grandma 
wants a successor, doesn't she?

135
00:10:44,190 --> 00:10:49,960
I get not wanting to make her sad, 
but it has to end someday.

136
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:54,340
Oh, but I'm not saying this 
to be territorial or anything.

137
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:56,340
I'm just worried about the two of you.

138
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:56,340
I'm just worried about
the two of you...

139
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,740
I promise I'll do the right thing.

140
00:10:58,740 --> 00:10:59,810
Huh?

141
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:02,780
For you and for Mizuhara.

142
00:11:04,050 --> 00:11:07,440
I'll find a way to end it in a way 
that doesn't make anyone unhappy.

143
00:11:11,470 --> 00:11:13,780
You'd better call your 
grandma right away, then.

144
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:15,580
Huh? Where'd that come from?

145
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:17,030
What are you saying?

146
00:11:17,430 --> 00:11:20,570
You have the cutest 
li'l girlfriend right here!

147
00:11:20,570 --> 00:11:23,470
Okay, but that's a different matter.

148
00:11:23,470 --> 00:11:26,600
<i>I was worried things 
would stay like this forever.</i>

149
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:30,880
<i>Because I really, really love him.</i>

150
00:11:33,450 --> 00:11:35,470
Prove it by kissing.

151
00:11:44,410 --> 00:11:46,820
Wh-What are you saying, Mami-chan?

152
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,810
Kiss? In front of everyone?

153
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:53,780
We're in public, too. 
There's no way we could kiss.

154
00:11:50,390 --> 00:11:53,230
<i>What is all this? What is going on?</i>

155
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:55,270
<i>The secret's out?</i>

156
00:11:55,270 --> 00:12:00,220
<i>His grandma and everyone else knows 
Chizuru-san's a rental girlfriend?</i>

157
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,740
<i>And "kiss," she says?!</i>

158
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:04,240
<i>She knows they can't do it.</i>

159
00:12:04,690 --> 00:12:06,780
<i>Did she drop her phone on purpose?</i>

160
00:12:07,230 --> 00:12:10,210
<i>Granny Nagomi's trying 
to air it all out, too.</i>

161
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:10,210
Rental Girlfriend

162
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:12,420
<i>Right here and now.</i>

163
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:15,960
But let's say I do snitch. 
What will you do then?

164
00:12:17,690 --> 00:12:21,200
<i>What do I do now?</i>

165
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:28,250
<i>That's obvious! I just have to do nothing!</i>

166
00:12:28,250 --> 00:12:32,020
<i>As long as I keep quiet and watch, 
their fake relationship will end.</i>

167
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:35,360
<i>I have no reason to help 
Kazuya-kun and Chizuru-san here!</i>

168
00:12:35,970 --> 00:12:40,200
<i>He's the one I've been 
looking for all my life!</i>

169
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:43,700
<i>I need him far more than Chizuru-san does!</i>

170
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:46,440
<i>It's their fault to begin with.</i>

171
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:50,550
<i>They kept dragging it out 
and putting it off!</i>

172
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:54,290
I'll find a way to end it in a way that 
doesn't make anyone unhappy.

173
00:12:55,070 --> 00:12:57,520
<i>Listen, Kazuya-kun.</i>

174
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:00,600
<i>You and I are meant to be.</i>

175
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:04,680
<i>We are each other's one and only 
soulmate in the whole wide world.</i>

176
00:13:05,710 --> 00:13:10,420
<i>Is it mean of me to think you should 
just "break it off" with Chizuru-san?</i>

177
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:16,530
<i>Is it so bad to wish that you 
be mine and mine alone?</i>

178
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,660
<i>I'll give you my all!</i>

179
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:22,990
<i>I'll do everything I can to make you 
fall in love with me for real!</i>

180
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:26,620
<i>So forgive me, Kazuya-kun.</i>

181
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,030
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

182
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:41,840
Let me ask you just one more thing.

183
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:47,190
Why did you invite me along on this trip?

184
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:52,200
I think I'm being a huge bother, honestly.

185
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:57,970
I mean, I'm a pathological liar, and I'm 
always following those two around.

186
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:02,830
I'm sure you'd rather 
be talking to Chizuru.

187
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:07,910
Even if I am her friend, 
there was no need to invite me.

188
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:11,250
If it was me, I wouldn't have.

189
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:19,550
Oh, is that all? 
The answer's a simple one.

190
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:23,620
Because I like you too, Ruka-dono.

191
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:26,960
I love your spirited voice 
and your beaming smile.

192
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:30,490
Just spending time with you 
makes me feel younger.

193
00:14:30,890 --> 00:14:35,120
And I've grown awfully 
fond of you, as well.

194
00:14:35,730 --> 00:14:39,690
Your tendency to lie seems to have 
died down a little lately, too.

195
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:41,510
O-Oh, well...

196
00:14:46,810 --> 00:14:50,830
Excuse me. We ask that you not cause 
a scene and bother the other guests.

197
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:53,360
Our apologies to the staff.

198
00:14:54,030 --> 00:14:56,790
But please give us just a moment.

199
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,450
We only need a few seconds.

200
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,210
Do it, Kazuya.

201
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:16,390
W-Wait, everyone. You look scary.

202
00:15:16,710 --> 00:15:21,570
They said they're dating, 
so what's the problem?

203
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:30,450
They say they're really together now, 
so what's the big deal?

204
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:32,540
<i>Ruka-chan!</i>

205
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,500
Yeah, exactly.

206
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:37,620
We're getting cold again.

207
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:37,620
We just got out
of the hot bath, too

208
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:37,620
November is November

209
00:15:38,130 --> 00:15:41,640
How about we get changed 
and settle down first?

210
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,590
<i>Kuri!</i>

211
00:15:43,070 --> 00:15:44,980
What are you saying, Shun-kun?

212
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:47,870
This isn't the time.

213
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,570
I-I get it. I do, okay?

214
00:15:51,570 --> 00:15:54,430
B-But nobody's thinking 
straight right now.

215
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:57,210
And, like, who'd kiss out here?

216
00:15:57,210 --> 00:15:59,270
Anyone would find that off-putting.

217
00:15:59,550 --> 00:16:02,990
Let's forget all this 
and hit up the arcade!

218
00:16:02,570 --> 00:16:08,990
I want some sticker pics

219
00:16:02,990 --> 00:16:05,090
I wanna play some token games!

220
00:16:05,090 --> 00:16:08,990
Good idea! Like that one with 
the dinosaur spitting out tokens!

221
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:11,660
Wait, that's a thing?!

222
00:16:09,330 --> 00:16:11,430
<i>Ruka-chan... Kuri...</i>

223
00:16:11,430 --> 00:16:13,950
<i>You guys... You guys!</i>

224
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:13,950
Let's try to hit the jackpot!

225
00:16:14,370 --> 00:16:16,780
I'm super good at crane games, too!

226
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:19,670
Wow, get me something!

227
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,630
Sheesh.

228
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,780
Isn't this your third rejection?

229
00:16:26,370 --> 00:16:28,590
How are you still crying that much?

230
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:33,640
I mean, she used to say it was great 
how I didn't give up on her!

231
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:35,560
Within limits, yeah, sure.

232
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:40,020
Don't you get that she's out
of your league, you moron?!

233
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:38,430
This is one you should give up on.

234
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:40,020
Give up
after one try

235
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:39,590
Really?

236
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:44,990
Everyone comes up with BS to say quick 
between your message and theirs.

237
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:45,980
They act like life is a game
in which they score points
by making people happy

238
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:45,980
Girls use the heart emoji
like we think of the star emoji

239
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,920
You know that's how it works.

240
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,770
We all try not to be hated, 
not to take things at face value,

241
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:53,950
not to suck up too much, 
and not to leave awkward pauses.

242
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:58,830
It's a neverending cycle of trivial lies. 
That's the basis of human relationships.

243
00:17:02,110 --> 00:17:05,780
I'm not letting her sell me 
a bridge or whatever, okay?

244
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,330
I wanted to believe in her 
because I like her.

245
00:17:11,970 --> 00:17:17,120
I'm saying there's a limit realistically 
to how much you can trust a person.

246
00:17:25,410 --> 00:17:29,110
Anyway, cheer up. I'll treat you 
to a beef bowl or whatever.

247
00:17:29,110 --> 00:17:30,330
Wow, you're a god.

248
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:37,160
Watching you does make me feel like 
I want to be friends with believers.

249
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:39,520
Kibe...

250
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:42,860
Order a salad too, 
and our friendship is over.

251
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:44,560
So I'm on thin ice?

252
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:49,740
A-Achoo. Yikes, I might've 
caught a cold out here.

253
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:52,510
That's not good! Let's hit 
the locker rooms right away!

254
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,110
Kuri, Sarashina-san.

255
00:17:58,030 --> 00:17:59,560
Please shut up for a second.

256
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:15,820
This might be crude of me, 
but I don't want to be tricked any more.

257
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:19,600
There's a limit to how much 
one person can trust another.

258
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:21,830
After lying to me for a year and a half,

259
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:25,700
if you're still out here 
trying to keep up the lie...

260
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:29,310
then you're no longer the Kinoshita 
Kazuya I called my best friend.

261
00:18:30,530 --> 00:18:32,900
I'm not saying I like 
suspecting Chizuru-san,

262
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:36,430
but Nagomi-san wants you to be 
happy more than anyone else,

263
00:18:36,430 --> 00:18:39,400
and I think she should be 
just as important to you.

264
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:43,830
Look, Kazuya. For fifteen years,

265
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:47,120
I've thought you were
a moron countless times,

266
00:18:48,410 --> 00:18:51,820
but I've never once 
thought of you as a liar.

267
00:18:53,390 --> 00:18:54,530
And you're not, are you?

268
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:18,930
<i>I want to die.</i>

269
00:19:20,210 --> 00:19:23,230
<i>I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!</i>

270
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:27,690
<i>This is all my fault.</i>

271
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:31,270
<i>If only I hadn't tried 
to act cool back then...</i>

272
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:34,420
<i>If only I hadn't said 
she was my girlfriend...</i>

273
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:38,200
<i>If only I hadn't rented 
Mizuhara out for that...</i>

274
00:19:38,990 --> 00:19:43,490
<i>If only I hadn't let Ruka-chan 
talk me into trying out dating her...</i>

275
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:47,960
<i>If only I hadn't gotten carried away 
and booked a double date with Kuri...</i>

276
00:19:48,890 --> 00:19:51,500
<i>If only I'd told Dad the truth...</i>

277
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:53,920
<i>If only I'd told Mom 
that it was all lies...</i>

278
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:57,440
<i>I'm really sorry.</i>

279
00:19:57,440 --> 00:20:01,230
<i>I'm really, really sorry for everything!</i>

280
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:15,270
<i>In that moment,</i>

281
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,740
<i>so many thoughts crossed my mind.</i>

282
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:21,200
<i>"I'm truly sorry, Mizuhara."</i>

283
00:22:24,530 --> 00:22:27,820
<i>"How did Mami-chan react?"</i>

284
00:22:28,950 --> 00:22:32,460
<i>"I told Gran a massive lie again."</i>

285
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:41,210
<i>"Kibe, you'll always be my best friend, 
no matter what."</i>

286
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:47,100
<i>"Kuri, can you believe this?"</i>

287
00:22:50,450 --> 00:22:53,810
<i>"Ruka-chan must be fuming."</i>

288
00:22:57,270 --> 00:22:58,280
<i>But...</i>

289
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:09,000
<i>The main one was 
"Then, now, and forever...</i>

290
00:23:31,490 --> 00:23:34,190
<i>My world always revolves around you."</i>

291
00:23:35,090 --> 00:23:36,490
<i>That realization hit me.</i>

292
00:23:45,990 --> 00:23:56,910
Rent-a-Girlfriend

293
00:23:57,730 --> 00:23:59,920
Whoa, I'm blushing hard!

294
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:03,850
Huh? Did we just kiss?!

295
00:24:04,170 --> 00:24:05,550
Am I dreaming?

296
00:24:05,550 --> 00:24:08,430
That's right, Kazu-chin. 
It was all a dream.

297
00:24:08,430 --> 00:24:09,510
Kibe...

298
00:24:09,510 --> 00:24:11,390
Wait, there's no way.

299
00:24:11,390 --> 00:24:13,580
Just think about it. A fool like you?

300
00:24:13,580 --> 00:24:16,770
Get a lovely girlfriend like 
Chizuru-san? Not a chance.

301
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:18,950
N-No...

302
00:24:18,950 --> 00:24:21,670
So everything up until now was a dream?

303
00:24:21,670 --> 00:24:23,440
So, next time on <i>Rent-a-Girlfriend</i>:

304
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:26,940
"Legitimate Girlfriend"

305
00:24:23,830 --> 00:24:25,210
"Legitimate...

306
00:24:25,210 --> 00:24:26,300
...Girlfriend."

